? Team health checks give teams a quick, regular self-assessment that highlights trends and areas for improvement.

@@ BE6 | Hybrid
The organisation's projects consistently underestimate their durations. Which technique adjusts estimates using the actual outcomes of similar past projects?
A) Reference class forecasting
B) Resource smoothing
C) Rolling wave planning
D) Critical chain buffering
= A
? Reference class forecasting bases estimates on the actual results of a class of similar projects, which corrects optimism bias.

@@ BE7 | Predictive
Employees resist the new office's shared desks, which were introduced for hybrid working. What should the project do?
A) Explain the reasons, involve employees in designing team zones, and pilot the layout
B) Remove the employees' old desks over a weekend, so that they have no choice but to adapt
C) Return to fixed desks for everyone, since employees will never accept sharing desks
D) Announce that desk use will be monitored and reported to the employees' managers
= A
? Involvement, explanation and piloting address the reasons for resistance and allow the new way of working to be adapted to people's needs.

@@ BE7 | Agile
Artists resist moving to a new game engine because they are experts in the old tools. What should the studio do?
A) Provide training and time to learn, with senior artists as mentors
B) Switch to the new engine immediately and require the artists to adapt within a week
C) Let each artist decide whether to use the old or the new engine on the project
D) Replace the artists who resist with new artists who already know the new engine
= A
? Change temporarily reduces productivity. Training, mentoring and realistic expectations help people through the transition.

@@ BE7 | Hybrid
Some department heads publicly support the new process but tell their teams privately to keep using the old one. What should the project manager do?
A) Raise it with the sponsor and the leaders to align their messages and behaviour
B) Ignore it, since the department heads support the process in public
C) Tell the teams to ignore their department heads' private instructions and follow the process
D) Report the department heads to the board without speaking to them first
= A
