@@ BE7 | Predictive
Labour law requires consultation with employee representatives before work practices are changed. What should the project do?
A) Plan and hold the consultation before implementing the change
B) Implement the change first and consult the representatives afterwards
C) Consult only the managers, since they will implement the change
D) Avoid the consultation by describing the change as a pilot
= A
? Legal consultation requirements are planned into the change, with enough time for genuine consultation before implementation.

@@ BE7 | Agile | multi
Six months into a transformation, enthusiasm is fading. Which two actions help sustain momentum? (Choose two.)
A) Making short-term wins visible and celebrating them
B) Using early successes to drive further improvements
C) Declaring the transformation complete
D) Reducing communication about the change
E) Disbanding the group leading the change
= A, B
? Visible short-term wins maintain energy, and consolidating gains to produce more change prevents a return to old habits (Kotter's steps 6 and 7).

@@ BE8 | Agile
A major platform announces that it will change its payment rules, which affects the game's in-game purchases. What should the product owner do?
